  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Family Planning Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Integrated Family Planning project aims at increasing the availability of contraceptive methods in two provinces, as well as re-positioning of family planning in the broader development agenda. Four districts in each of the two most populous provinces (Zambezia and Nampula) benefit from facility and community-based provision of different family planning methods including the pilot of self-injected contraceptives. The purpose is to use these two sites to drive broader reforms and efficiency gains across the country in the areas of family planning. The component also includes an objective to secure a commitment from the Government of Mozambique to increase domestic financing for family planning commodities in the short to medium term, and to make family planning a part of the multisectoral policy dialogue.</narrative>
  </description>
